<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-18">18 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Clyde Tombaugh discovers Pluto</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Comparing photographic plates at Lowell Observatory, Tombaugh found a faint moving object. Named Pluto at the suggestion of 11-year-old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venetia">Venetia</a> Burney, it was reclassified as a dwarf planet in 2006.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venetia">Venetia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-2">2 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">D. H. Lawrence dies in the south of France</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The author of 'Sons and Lovers' and 'Lady Chatterley's Lover' died of tuberculosis at Vence, aged 44. 'Lady Chatterley' was not published openly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> until the 1960 obscenity trial.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-6">6 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Clarence Birdseye's frozen foods go on sale</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Shops in Springfield, Massachusetts, began selling quick-frozen vegetables, fruit, fish and meat using Birdseye's process. Frozen food went on to transform shopping and diets.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-6">6 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Gandhi breaks the salt law at Dandi</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At the end of his 24-day march to the sea, Mohandas <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Gandhi</a> picked up a lump of natural salt at Dandi, defying the British monopoly. The gesture launched a mass campaign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/civil-disobedience">civil disobedience</a> across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/haile-selassie.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-2">2 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Haile Selassie is crowned Emperor of Ethiopia</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ras">Ras</a> Tafari Makonnen was crowned Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a> I in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addis-ababa">Addis Ababa</a> before foreign dignitaries. He ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, with an interruption during Italian occupation, until his overthrow in 1974.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addis-ababa">Addis Ababa</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/salt-march" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/salt-march.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/salt-march">Salt March</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Salt March was a campaign of civil disobedience led by Mahatma Gandhi in British India in 1930.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/yen-bai-mutiny">Yên Bái mutiny</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Yên Bái mutiny was an uprising on the night of 9–10 February 1930 in which Vietnamese colonial soldiers at the garrison of Yên Bái in northern Vietnam, organised by the Vietnamese Nationalist Party, attacked their French officers.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/wushe-incident" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wushe-incident.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/wushe-incident">Wushe Incident</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Wushe Incident (Musha Incident) was an uprising of Seediq people against Japanese colonial rule at Wushe (Musha) in central Taiwan in October 1930.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/anglo-iraqi-treaty-1930">Anglo-Iraqi Treaty (1930)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Anglo-Iraqi Treaty of 1930 was an alliance signed between Britain and the Kingdom of Iraq, then under a League of Nations mandate.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/tilari-massacre">Tilari massacre</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Tilari massacre took place on 30 May 1930 at Tilari, in the Rawain area of Tehri Garhwal State in the Himalaya, when the state's troops fired on villagers gathered to protest new forest rules that restricted their customary rights.</p></div></li></ol></section>
